{title: Hymn of Promise}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
In the [C]bulb there is a [**]flower; in the [Dm]seed, an apple [**]tree
In co[G]coons, a hidden [**]promise: butter[C]flies will soon be [C7]free!
In the [F]cold and snow of [Em]winter there's a [Dm]spring that waits to [Am]be
Unre[F]vealed until its [C]season, something [Dm]God alone can [C]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There's a [C]song in every [**]silence, seeking [Dm]word and melo[**]dy
There's a [G]dawn in every [**]darkness, bringing [C]hope to you and [C7]me
From the [F]past will come the [Em]future; what it [Dm]holds, a myste[Am]ry
Unre[F]vealed until its [C]season, something [Dm]God alone can [C]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In our [C]end is our be[**]ginning; in our [Dm]time, infini[**]ty
In our [G]doubt there is be[**]lieving; in our [C]life, eterni[C7]ty
In our [F]death, a resur[Em]rection; at the [Dm]last, a victo[Am]ry
Unre[F]vealed until its [C]season, something [Dm]God alone can [C]see.
{end_of_verse}
